tinuedAt="Tb_XK7waXqqsUSzfOUqvVtlGw_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">NOTE&#160;7&#160;&#8212; TAXES</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="display:inline-block;text-indent:0pt;width:18pt;"><b style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;">(a)</b></span>Corporate<span style="font-weight:normal;"> </span>Income<span style="font-weight:normal;"> </span>Taxes<span style="font-weight:normal;"> </span>(&#8220;CIT&#8221;)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Cayman Islands</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Under the current tax laws of the Cayman Islands, the Company is not subject to tax on its income or capital gains. In addition, no Cayman Islands withholding tax will be imposed upon the payment of dividends by the Company to its shareholders.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">Hong Kong</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">YSX HK was incorporated in Hong Kong and is subject to profit taxes in Hong Kong at a rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_dZ4FdQwVNk-ZA8lLEwJFLw" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_i-HJiRroTEi1xEGBSTRMfg">16.5</ix:nonFraction>%. However, YSX HK did not generate any assessable profits arising in or derived from Hong Kong for the fiscal years ended March 31, 2026, 2025 and 2024, and accordingly <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_yovK8iPZ_EedJPURUVJWjg" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2023_To_3_31_2024_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_JzZkflwQMEKtmos8ldsSdg" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxExpenseBenefit" scale="0" id="Narr_Imic4kYQDEm-5ZagA5xBvg"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_yovK8iPZ_EedJPURUVJWjg" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2024_To_3_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_JT43LbubSkONqNX73p4rbw" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxExpenseBenefit" scale="0" id="Narr_G1KZifiR8EumkPo-l1aHkw"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_yovK8iPZ_EedJPURUVJWjg" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_dZ4FdQwVNk-ZA8lLEwJFLw" decimals="0" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxExpenseBenefit" scale="0" id="Narr_tDM7zFXHg0-8LUF6zdrVMA">no</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction> provision for Hong Kong profits tax has been made in these periods.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-weight:normal;text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:underline;text-decoration-style:solid;">PRC</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Under the Enterprise Income Tax (&#8220;EIT&#8221;) Law of the PRC, domestic enterprises and Foreign Investment Enterprises (the &#8220;FIE&#8221;) are normally subject to a unified&#160;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_CN_-k3mcyAok0mCnNvJKkhUQQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_KiYZk3SBIUWIswPhv19_XQ">25</ix:nonFraction>% enterprise income tax rate while preferential tax rates, tax holidays, or exemptions may be granted on a case-by-case basis. The Company&#8217;s VIE entity Xinjiang YSX and its subsidiary Chuangzhan are all incorporated in Kashi city of Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region, where tax reduction and exemption policies were adopted and promulgated by local government to grant qualified enterprises enterprise income tax exemption for the first <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_dei_LegalEntityAxis_YSXT_XinjiangYsxAndSubsidiariesMember_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_YSXT_FirstFiveYearsOfTaxReductionMember_D3BykLEmSEOLsinQLd5r3Q" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="YSXT:QualifiedEnterprisesIncomeTaxExemptionPeriod" id="Narr_Y-_BuoVpm0utcmhATjOcrQ">five&#160;years</ix:nonNumeric> and a reduced corporate income tax of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MinimumMember_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_YSXT_AfterFiveYearsMember_dJbDLsy3MkW7uUwWwMkUlg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_gGw2OmDhFUejcgmUXkQP7g">10</ix:nonFraction>% to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_YSXT_AfterFiveYearsMember_LFaOqUYAAEWks44IrEa4ug" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_zK_w9O2X8U2rFOO-RCCX4g">15</ix:nonFraction>% thereafter, as an incentive to attract enterprises to establish their business operations in such region and to stimulate local economic development. As a result, Xinjiang YSX is subject to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_dei_LegalEntityAxis_YSXT_XinjiangYishengxinNetworkTechnologyCoLtdMember_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_YSXT_AfterFiveYearsMember_03EYmDKtfUyS6MBJkMxkcg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_z1robiz7A0WNoAvvg8pimA">15</ix:nonFraction>% income tax rate starting from January&#160;2021. Chuangzhan is entitled to income tax exemption from 2021 to 2025 and has been subject to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_dei_LegalEntityAxis_YSXT_XinjiangYishengxinChuangzhanTechnologyCoLtdMember_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_YSXT_AfterFiveYearsMember_GCtCc41qNUuvbPHpdfyFng" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_qI6eSvyRckuGOihdLuwECQ">15</ix:nonFraction>% income tax rate starting from January&#160;2026. In addition, EIT grants preferential tax treatment to High and New Technology Enterprises (&#8220;HNTEs&#8221;). Under this preferential tax treatment, HNTEs are entitled to an income tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_PnQPQdomt0qMvPnRhXbbeg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="YSXT:HighAndNewTechnologyEnterprisesTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_5URXkOw1g0yVoVUArPeOwQ">15</ix:nonFraction>%, subject to a requirement that they re-apply for their HNTE status every three&#160;years. EIT is typically governed by the local tax authority in PRC. Each local tax authority at times may grant tax holidays to local enterprises as a way to encourage entrepreneurship and stimulate local economy. The Company&#8217;s another VIE, Xihang, was approved as a HNTE on December&#160;20, 2021 and was entitled to a reduced income tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_dei_LegalEntityAxis_YSXT_GuangzhouXihangInformationTechnologyCoLtdMember_4gYblnO7oEymbUf0WF-VTA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="YSXT:HighAndNewTechnologyEnterprisesTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_2RSCNGmL4UKClUedqBRY3Q">15</ix:nonFraction>% with a term of <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_dei_LegalEntityAxis_YSXT_GuangzhouXihangInformationTechnologyCoLtdMember_4gYblnO7oEymbUf0WF-VTA" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="YSXT:HighAndNewTechnologyEnterprisesStatusExpirationPeriod" id="Narr_BRWjnMwiOEG3hlciFO-1Yw">three&#160;years</ix:nonNumeric>. Xihang filed an application with the local tax authority in December 2024 to renew its HNTE certificate, which was approved in December 2025. In addition, Xinjiang YSX&#8217;s subsidiary, YSX Network, is located in Guangzhou city of Guangdong province, was also approved as a HNTE in December 2025 and is now subject to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_dei_LegalEntityAxis_YSXT_GuangzhouYishengxinNetworkTechnologyCoLtdMember_z5JOFQZBuU-4EzFMM1BARA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="YSXT:HighAndNewTechnologyEnterprisesTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_A4kvwOdrgkSCbuAggBSsAQ">15</ix:nonFraction>% favorable income tax rate for <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_dei_LegalEntityAxis_YSXT_GuangzhouYishengxinNetworkTechnologyCoLtdMember_z5JOFQZBuU-4EzFMM1BARA" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="YSXT:HighAndNewTechnologyEnterprisesStatusExpirationPeriod" id="Narr_qc9pTuJrvkqMwhGfFW4uLw">three years</ix:nonNumeric>.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As a result of the above, the Company&#8217;s corporate income taxes for the years ended March 31, 2026, 2025 and 2024 were reported at a blended reduced rate. The impact of the tax holidays and exemptions noted above decreased PRC corporate income taxes by $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_yovK8iPZ_EedJPURUVJWjg" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_PnQPQdomt0qMvPnRhXbbeg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxHolidayAggregateDollarAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_24Dh6HFDFE61AiHZmoq_Ag">510,152</ix:nonFraction>, $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_yovK8iPZ_EedJPURUVJWjg" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2024_To_3_31_2025_ZwZNJj2cwkeF0vyGXfbeug" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxHolidayAggregateDollarAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_hWMrlkjcvk-seRgrCB0lHA">497,396</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_yovK8iPZ_EedJPURUVJWjg" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2023_To_3_31_2024_QAZmCuHDU0CVxbM1PbMIqg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxHolidayAggregateDollarAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_xiRt20B4rUOYAgzIb19ebQ">413,403</ix:nonFraction> for the years ended March 31, 2026, 2025 and 2024, respectively. The benefit of the tax holidays on net income per share (basic and diluted) of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ue62wJF5HUyYPBS2QRX0YQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_PnQPQdomt0qMvPnRhXbbeg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxHolidayIncomeTaxBenefitsPerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_MiUbytEjo0OTbyo6hvikdw">0.03</ix:nonFraction>, $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ue62wJF5HUyYPBS2QRX0YQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2024_To_3_31_2025_ZwZNJj2cwkeF0vyGXfbeug" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxHolidayIncomeTaxBenefitsPerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_u6uBsYInZE6mRNIfqHbrkg">0.02</ix:nonFraction> and $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ue62wJF5HUyYPBS2QRX0YQ" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2023_To_3_31_2024_QAZmCuHDU0CVxbM1PbMIqg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:IncomeT