j-4ufkihv3ZjK4ULkQ" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_jPP90L0K2EaUYW0YSEHmoQ">1,378,037</ix:nonFraction>) for three years, with loan maturity date on June 2, 2026. The loan bears interest at a variable rate calculated based on the prevailing interest rates set by the People&#8217;s Bank of China at the time of borrowing, plus <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="Duration_6_3_2023_To_6_3_2023_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_YSXT_LoanFromGzRuralBankMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_srt_BoardOfDirectorsChairmanMember_AHUL1u1vIkaK4_yeriApUg" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentBasisSpreadOnVariableRate1" scale="-4" id="Narr_ZYFPglvfy0yrjx2USU9aew">55</ix:nonFraction> basis points, and the effective interest rate is <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_rrae3UlHvU-oC0aCapvvoQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_2_2023_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_YSXT_LoanFromGzRuralBankMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_srt_BoardOfDirectorsChairmanMember_mryRmAp4BU6uf3v4ElH-ag" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateEffectivePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_De12D9VOwUiVuPK64Xvmog">4.10</ix:nonFraction>% per annum. Xinjiang YSX and its branch company Guangzhou YSX provided guarantee to this loan. The Company&#8217;s shareholder Mr. Weiqiang Zhen pledged his personal assets as collateral with GZ Rural Bank to further secure this loan. At the same time, the Company signed a loan agreement with Mr. Jie Xiao to borrow the RMB <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_uuxYecw-eUyXXJZ-h67xpQ" contextRef="As_Of_6_2_2023_dei_LegalEntityAxis_YSXT_MrJieXiaoMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_kW06E5DNKUywjPiXyhIfJg" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_1Uw85RBQyk2y5SFAn_EkiA">10</ix:nonFraction> million (approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_yovK8iPZ_EedJPURUVJWjg" contextRef="As_Of_6_2_2023_dei_LegalEntityAxis_YSXT_MrJieXiaoMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_kW06E5DNKUywjPiXyhIfJg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="0" id="Narr_ttvUBC4SvUqpJQJePz_aHw">1,378,037</ix:nonFraction>) with the same borrowing terms and interest rate. The purpose of this borrowing is to obtain funds to support the Company&#8217;s working capital needs, especially for making payments to external vendors to perform the outsourced value-added services. The loan was fully repaid as of March 31, 2025. There was no such related party loan as of March 31, 2026.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">f</span><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">. </span><b style="font-weight:bold;">Loan guarantees provided by related parties</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">From December 9, 2024 to January 2, 2025, YSX Network entered multiple loan agreements with China CITIC Bank to borrow an aggregate of loans of RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_uuxYecw-eUyXXJZ-h67xpQ" contextRef="As_Of_1_2_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_YSXT_GuangzhouYishengxinNetworkTechnologyCoLtdMember_us-gaap_DebtInstrumentAxis_YSXT_ShortTermLoanChinaCiticBankMember_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_tJqWRv76u0OO2oHLcGYkdQ" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="6" id="Narr_KDHgwcfwr0mv7lrKlc3FSA">10</ix:nonFraction> million (approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_yovK8iPZ_EedJPURUVJWjg" contextRef="As_Of_1_2_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameA