aymentArrangementEmployeeMember_0fqDSL4cd0mN_-1MzQ5GKQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="YSXT:NumberOfPersonsToWhomSharesGranted" scale="0" id="Narr_2ympM3QN_0CIml4jX32idA">eleven</ix:nonFraction> (11) employees for services to be rendered over a <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_9_30_2025_To_9_30_2025_us-gaap_GranteeStatusAxis_us-gaap_ShareBasedPaymentArrangementEmployeeMember_0fqDSL4cd0mN_-1MzQ5GKQ" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardAwardRequisiteServicePeriod1" id="Narr_mZI-MuQxFEmWMjGxQ_G4tg">four-year</ix:nonNumeric> service period. These shares were granted at the nominal par value of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ue62wJF5HUyYPBS2QRX0YQ" contextRef="As_Of_9_30_2025_us-gaap_GranteeStatusAxis_us-gaap_ShareBasedPaymentArrangementEmployeeMember_gXIUcy5-mU-Gwd64OzIt6Q" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockParOrStatedValuePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_12URQk3WAECcJrIomlRIbw">0.0001</ix:nonFraction> per ordinary share, with a grant-date fair value of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ue62wJF5HUyYPBS2QRX0YQ" contextRef="Duration_9_30_2025_To_9_30_2025_us-gaap_GranteeStatusAxis_us-gaap_ShareBasedPaymentArrangementEmployeeMember_0fqDSL4cd0mN_-1MzQ5GKQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardEquityInstrumentsOtherThanOptionsVestedInPeriodWeightedAverageGrantDateFairValue" scale="0" id="Narr_xI5rz-jaN0qrc1hbhMQ1_Q">2.72</ix:nonFraction> per ordinary share.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company accounts for share-based transactions with both employees and non-employees in accordance with <i style="font-style:italic;">ASC Topic 718, Compensation&#8212;Stock Compensation.</i> Under this standard, the framework for measuring non-employee consultant awards is fully aligned with employee guidelines. The Company measures the fair value of restricted stock awards based solely on the closing market price of the Company&#8217;s underlying ordinary shares on the date of grant. No option pricing models, such as the Black-Scholes-Merton formula, are utilized to value these awards. Because restricted stock awards represent outstanding equity instruments that carry no exercise price (the nominal par value of $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_ue62wJF5HUyYPBS2QRX0YQ" contextRef="As_Of_3_31_2026_ieA1VeS1lkGmm7KV1A9l-w" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:CommonStockParOrStatedValuePerShare" scale="0" id="Narr_RusLgpYE4UWF3VCNCA1ilA">0.0001</ix:nonFraction> per share being a capital settlement), the awards inherently possess the full value of a share of common stock upon the fulfillment of service conditions. Consequently, option volatility, dividend yields, and risk-free interest rates do not impact the measurement of these awards.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">For the <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_qbTeu3n2yEmrQO6IuoS81Q" contextRef="Duration_7_31_2025_To_7_31_2025_us-gaap_GranteeStatusAxis_us-gaap_ShareBasedPaymentArrangementNonemployeeMember_lNxWZVVRXE2jLqw_upMHzg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardEquityInstrumentsOtherThanOptionsVestedInPeriod" scale="0" id="Narr_qK1WXhcSckCQPscdHppJ3Q">210,000</ix:nonFraction> restricted shares that vested immediately on July 31, 2025, the full grant-date fair value of approximately $<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_yovK8iPZ_EedJPURUVJWjg" contextRef="Duration_7_31_2025_To_7_31_2025_us-gaap_GranteeStatusAxis_us-gaap_ShareBasedPaymentArrangementNonemployeeMember_lNxWZVVRXE2jLqw_upMHzg" decimals="0" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardEquityInstrumentsOtherThanOptionsVestedInPeriodTotalFairValue" scale="0" id="Narr_jqztxzk7TUKmd-uegck5Qw">630,000</ix:nonFraction> was recognized as compensation expense on the date of grant, as no future service period was required. For the remaining <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_shares_qbTeu3n2yEmrQO6IuoS81Q" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_PnQPQdomt0qMvPnRhXbbeg" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="YSXT:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardEquityInstrumentsOtherThanOptionsExpectedToVestOutstandingNumber" scale="0" id="Narr_iC5f-Vm0VESUzzSIWU3MyA">4,235,000</ix:nonFraction> shares containing service-only graded vesting conditions across <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_installment_zVTdrYROFEmdfaA4YkjDLw" contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_PnQPQdomt0qMvPnRhXbbeg" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="YSXT:NumberOfSemiAnnualVestingInstallments" scale="0" id="Narr_iR1oqL5eRUC4LuWUWukE8A">eight</ix:nonFraction> semi-annual installments, the Company has elected a single-option accounting policy under ASC 718-20-35-3 to recognize total stock compensation costs using the graded vesting attribution method over the entire <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_4_1_2025_To_3_31_2026_PnQPQdomt0qMvPnRhXbbeg" format="ixt-sec:durwordsen" name="us-gaap:ShareBasedCompensationArrangementByShareBasedPaymentAwardAwardRequisiteServicePeriod1" id="Narr_Ge7jNXcpCUqlYZNTCs2mJQ">4-year</ix:nonNumeric> requisite service lifecycle. Stock-based compensation expense is adjusted for actual forfeitures as they occur.</p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-33</p></div></div>
